---
description: Vendor-neutral agent instructions — defer to AGENTS.md
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository's canonical instructions live in `AGENTS.md` files (Cursor also reads
`AGENTS.md` natively; this rule is belt-and-suspenders).

- Repo-wide conventions: the root `AGENTS.md`.
- The agent you're working in: `agents/<name>/AGENTS.md`
  (e.g. `agents/job-application/AGENTS.md`).

Always read and follow the `AGENTS.md` nearest to the files you're editing. Key rules
that always hold: keep personal data out of git (real `config/config.yaml`,
`config/profiles/*.yaml`, and `output/` are gitignored — only the `example` templates
are tracked); stay human-in-the-loop (propose, don't auto-submit; never bypass
captchas/logins; never fabricate); keep agents self-contained.
